  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC PHASE-OUT MANAGEMENT PLAN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC PHASE-OUT MANAGEMENT PLAN HCFC phase-out strategy The Government of Bahrain is proposing to follow the Montreal Protocol schedule and to adopt a staged approach in order to achieve complete phase-out of HCFCs by 2030, except for a service tail to 2040. This submission only contains stage I of the HPMP to meet a 35 per cent reduction in consumption, as compared to the baseline, by 2020.  Specific activities: Activities realted to compliance Conversion of central AC line to HFC-410A/HFC-407C (UNIDO) Incremental operating cost for central AC calculated at US $6.3/kg for 6 months (UNIDO) Setting up a pre-production line for the conversion of small window AC units to HC-290 or HFC-32 (UNIDO) Conversion of small AC line to HFC-32 or HC-290 and training for servicing network (UNIDO) Incremental operating cost for split AC calculated at US $6.3/kg for six months (UNIDO)  Updating policy and regulations (UNEP) Technical assistance to the servicing sector, including updating vocational curriculum, developing standard, training of technicians (UNEP) National HCFC reclamation programme (UNIDO)  Activities not related to compliance Conversion of HCFC-141b in pre-blended polyols to cyclopentane at AGM (UNIDO) Technical assistance to the small consumers in the foam sector (UNIDO)  Co-ordinating activities Project impleme</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Montreal Protocol</narrative>
  </participating-org>
